course: dictionary
lesson: 14034
title: Many meanings of manifest
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word manifest can mean to show something clearly, so the sign of an illness can show itself. «The illness began to manifest as a red rash on her arm.» The rash showed itself clearly, so the word manifest tells you it appeared.
explain: Manifest can also be an adjective meaning clear and obvious to everyone. «Her delight was manifest in her big smile.» Her happiness was easy to see. Manifest can also be a noun: the official list of goods or passengers on a ship, plane or train. «The crew checked the passenger manifest before take-off.» Clues like passengers and take-off tell you it is a list.
explain: Some people use manifest in modern talk, as in «I'm manifesting a snow day!» This means they are wishing very hard for it. Wishing is a popular idea, but wishing alone does not make things happen. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Manifest can be a verb, an adjective or a noun.
fact: As a verb, «manifest» means to show clearly or to appear. «Symptoms manifest» means the signs of an illness show themselves.
fact: As an adjective, «manifest» means clear and obvious to everyone.
fact: As a noun, a manifest is the official list of goods or passengers on a ship, plane or train.
fact: Modern slang uses «manifesting» to mean wishing hard for something, but wishing alone does not make it happen.
exercise: «The fever began to manifest as a rash.» What does manifest mean here? | Was hidden from everyone | Tasted very sweet | *Showed itself clearly | Went away quickly
exercise: The ship's manifest was on the desk. What is a manifest? | A type of ship's sail | A map of the sea | A loud ship's horn | *A list of passengers or goods
exercise: «Her nerves were manifest on the stage.» What does manifest mean in this sentence? | Hidden and secret | Quiet and gentle | *Clear and obvious to everyone | Lost and missing
test: «Symptoms manifest when the illness begins.» What does manifest mean? | To cook slowly | To disappear completely | *To appear and show | To run away quickly
test: Jamal says, «I'm manifesting a snow day!» What does he mean? | *He is wishing hard for it | He is making the snow happen right now | He is feeling cold | He has a list of the snow
exam: Which sentence uses manifest as a noun? | «The rash will manifest by Monday.» | «Her joy was manifest on her face.» | *«The crew checked the passenger manifest before take-off.» | «The ghost began to manifest in the hall.»
